# Nehir skhd layer — binds hotkeys.toml can't express (docs/keybindings.md):
#   - a/d left-hand aliases for h/l focus/move: the hotkeys.toml codec maps
#     one chord per action id, so a second chord has to come from outside.
#   - r/Shift+r ratio splits: parameterized commands (set-column-width) have
#     no hotkeys.toml action id, so they route through nehir-ratio.sh.
#
# Absolute nehirctl path — the skhd agent's launchd PATH has no Homebrew bin
# dir. skhdrc loads this whenever nehir is *enabled* and skhd grabs at the
# event-tap level regardless of which WM runs, so under another WM these keys
# are dead rather than passed through.

alt - a : /Applications/Nehir.app/Contents/MacOS/nehirctl command focus left
alt - d : /Applications/Nehir.app/Contents/MacOS/nehirctl command focus right
shift + alt - a : /Applications/Nehir.app/Contents/MacOS/nehirctl command move left
shift + alt - d : /Applications/Nehir.app/Contents/MacOS/nehirctl command move right

# Ratio splits: focused column 2/3 and its neighbor 1/3; Shift = inverse.
# 50/50 is Option+B (balance-sizes) and full-width Option+W, both in
# hotkeys.toml — together the three width regimes: equal / asymmetric / all.
alt - r : sh ~/.config/skhd/nehir-ratio.sh 66.667% 33.333%
shift + alt - r : sh ~/.config/skhd/nehir-ratio.sh 33.333% 66.667%
